{
 "regions": {
  "r2": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "5. Intent upon propitiating them, I endured with great",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "difficulty the taunting words of wicked men; checking in",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "my tears I even laughed with a vacant mind; I steadied my",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "heart, and even bowed to the wicked. Disappointed Greed,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "in what other way wilt thou make me dance ?",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r3": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "6. For the sake of this life (lit. these vital airs) that is",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "compared to water on a lotus leaf, what, indeed, have we,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "destitute of discernment, not done ?—since in the presence",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "of the rich whose minds are blinded by the pride of wealth,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "we, shameless that we are, have committed the sin of even",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "mentioning (singing the praises of) our own virtues.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r4": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "7 We forbore but not through forgiveness; we relin-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "quished domestic happiness—but not willingly; we endured",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "the pain caused by inclement cold, wind and sun—but did",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "not (thereby) practise austerities; day and night did we",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "think of weath—but not, with restrained vital airs, of the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "feet of S'iva. We did the various actions which ascetics",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "perform; but as to the several fruits ( obtained by them ) we",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "have been deceived.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r5": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "8. We have not enjoyed pleasures, but we have been",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "preyed upon (by the destructive influence of time ); we have",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "not undergone austerities, but we have been harassed ( by",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "worldly cares); time has not lapsed, but the lease of our life;",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "our greed has not decayed but we have.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r6": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "9. Wrinkles have made an inroad on the face; the head",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "is marked ( with gray hair ) all the limbs become feeble;",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "greed alone keeps its vigour fresh.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r7": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "10. The desire for enjoyments is dead; the pride of youth",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "is quite: humbled co-eval, friends, valued as life itself, have",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "sped quick to heaven; ( I have ) to stand up slowly support-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "ed on a staff; and the eyes are obstructed by powerful",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r1": {
   "type": "page_number",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "[ 26 ]",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  }
 },
